// frontseat.runner.v1alpha1: what a worker's runner is told to start for a
// test. It is no API: nothing serves it and no client asks it. It is a
// file the daemon writes and the runner reads, both of this server, and
// its Go is theirs alone (server/internal/runnerapi).
//
// The test's service closure and its direct endpoint grants. The worker's
// runner makes separate sandboxes for the test and each service, each with
// a private loopback and no external network. The daemon says what to start,
// already resolved from Resource dependencies and API relationships,
// in the action's input root, at .frontseat/runtime/runner.binpb, so that
// it is part of the action's digest and nothing outside the Remote
// Execution API carries it; the runner reads it there.

